.\" Distro-authored man page for the Fedora pidp8i package.
.\" Candidate for upstreaming to the PiDP-8/I project.
.TH USB-MOUNT 1 "November 21, 2026" "PiDP-8/I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usb-mount \- mount and unmount USB media for the PiDP-8/I (udev helper)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-mount
{add|remove}
.I device_name
.RI "(e.g. sdb1)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usb-mount
is the helper behind the package's udev rule
.RI ( /etc/udev/rules.d/68-usb-mount.rules ):
when USB mass storage appears or disappears, udev runs it as
.B add
or
.B remove
with the device name, and it mounts or unmounts the device so that OS/8
media on it can be reached by the simulator's
.B load
and
.B dump
commands on a headless cabinet.
.PP
It is not meant to be run by hand; the
.B usb-mount@.service
template unit it triggers does the actual mounting. Members of the
.I pidp8i
group may use the companion poweroff and reboot commands through the
.I /etc/sudoers.d/pidp8i
rule.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/udev/rules.d/68-usb-mount.rules
the trigger
.TP
.B /usr/lib/systemd/system/usb-mount@.service
the instantiated mount service
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR udev (7),
.BR systemd (1)
